      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Taemwadjy\", \"choices\": [], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Tꜣ-mḏꜣ.t is the article tꜣ followed by mḏꜣ.t, rendered 'Ta-medjat'. Its consonants are t, m, ḏ, (ꜣ), t. Record 1, Taemwadjy, reads as Ta-em-wadjy, that is, tꜣ + m + wꜣḏ(y): 'she who is in the green/Wadjet'. This has a w between m and dj that C1 lacks, and an added consonant is not allowed. The words also differ: record 1 has the preposition m and a wꜣḏ word, while C1 has the single noun mḏꜣ.t. So record 1 cannot be read as C1's words, and C1 is not the same name.\"}"
